        "procedure": "Compound 1, [Dy3(HL)(H2L)(NO3)4]·C2H5OH, was prepared by the previously reported procedure. Crystals of 1 were placed in 30 mL of acetone at room temperature. After five days, the needle-like crystals of 1 had converted into block crystals of 2 by solvent exchange. The main text additionally states that the transformation is reversible: 2 returns to 1 on heating at 373 K in ethanol. No yield is reported.",
