      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Compound 2 is a triangular Dy3 single-molecule toroic/SMM. χMT is 43.26 cm3 K mol−1 at 300 K under 0.1 T, falls to 9.94 cm3 K mol−1 at 2 K, and shows a maximum near 4.5 K. Magnetization does not saturate by 7 T and no hysteresis is observed at 2 K. Zero-field ac susceptibility shows two relaxation processes; Table S3 assigns the faster process to Raman plus Orbach relaxation (Ueff = 72.0 cm−1) and the slower process to QTM plus Orbach relaxation (Ueff = 59.0 cm−1). The main text instead describes the slow process as Raman/Orbach and the fast process as QTM/Orbach.",
